values ('c3d4e5f6-7a8b-4c11-8d01-1e2f3a4b5c31', 'critical-thinking-logic', 'Critical Thinking / Logic', 'Students identify, reconstruct, and evaluate arguments in ordinary language, academic writing, media, and public debate; distinguish deductive validity, soundness, inductive strength, cogency, causal support, analogy, and explanatory reasoning; use basic propositional logic, truth tables, and proof patterns; recognize fallacies, cognitive biases, rhetorical manipulation, ambiguity, and weak evidence; evaluate sources, testimony, expertise, probability, statistics, scientific claims, and misinformation; and write clear analytical arguments with objections, replies, evidence, citations, and revision.');

